SUMMARY:🌆THE PATH\, CIBC SQUARE & WATERFRONT SUMMER EVENING WALK! 🌆
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🌆THE PATH\, CIBC SQUARE & WAT
 ERFRONT SUMMER EVENING WALK! 🌆\n\n**Escape the Heat\, Explore Toronto's
  Underground City & End the Night by the Lake**\nWhen Toronto gets hot\, t
 he smartest place to explore isn't always outside.\n\nJoin us for a summer
  evening adventure through **PATH**\, Toronto's incredible underground cit
 y — a 30-kilometre network of tunnels\, office towers\, shopping\, food 
 courts\, and hidden passageways connecting more than 70 downtown buildings
 .\nWe'll spend much of the evening enjoying the cool\, air-conditioned spa
 ces before making our way to one of Toronto's newest public spaces: **CIBC
  Square Park**\, an elevated urban park built above the railway tracks wit
 h incredible views of the city.\n\nTo finish the evening\, we'll head down
  to Toronto's beautiful waterfront where those who would like can grab a *
 *BeaverTail**\, relax by the lake\, and enjoy one of the best summer eveni
 ngs the city has to offer.\n\nThis isn't a historical tour.\n\nIt's a soci
 al walk\, an urban adventure\, and a great excuse to escape the summer hea
 t while discovering parts of downtown many people have never seen.\n\n📲
  **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join](https://chat.whatsapp.c
 om/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'
 ll begin at **Wellesley Subway Station** before making our way west and th
 en south toward the PATH system.\nOnce underground we'll weave our way thr
 ough Toronto's famous underground city\, discovering hidden corridors\, of
 fice towers\, shopping areas\, and the unique network that keeps downtown 
 moving year-round.\nFrom there we'll visit **CIBC Square Park**\, Toronto'
 s beautiful new elevated park built above the rail corridor\, offering spe
 ctacular views over Union Station and the surrounding skyline.\nFinally we
 'll stroll down to the waterfront where we'll relax beside Lake Ontario.\n
 If you'd like\, we'll grab a BeaverTail and spend a little time enjoying t
 he evening before heading home.\nExpect about **2½ to 3 hours** of walkin
 g at a comfortable social pace.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Expectations
 \n\nThis walk happens rain or shine.\nOne of the best parts of this event 
 is that much of our route is indoors in the cool PATH system\, making it t
 he perfect escape from hot summer days.\nPlease wear comfortable walking s
 hoes\, as we'll still be covering several kilometres.\nThis is a social wa
 lk—not a guided historical tour.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n**
 📍 Meetup Location:** Main entrance of Wellesley Subway Station (near th
 e PRESTO machines)\n🫎 I'll be wearing my **Moose Hat**\n**⏰ Meetup Ti
 me:** **6:30 PM**\n**I will only wait 5 minutes.**\nEarly is on time.\nOn 
 time is late.\nWe will leave promptly and won't be able to spend time help
 ing late arrivals catch up.\n**🏁 End Spot:** Toronto Waterfront\n\n***\
 n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **[m
 athewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\nThis fee he
 lps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events like thi
 s. Thank you for supporting community! 💖\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Brin
 g\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n💳 Spending money if yo
 u'd like a BeaverTail\n🧥 A light sweater (the PATH can feel cool)\n\n**
 *\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis group is open to anyone who wants to
  be social and make friends—whether single or not.\nWe also host:\n🎬 
 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture outings\n🍽️ Restauran
 t gatherings\nThere's always something happening.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** 
 You're welcome to just show up on the day if you're unsure about your sche
 dule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled\, so pl
 ease keep an eye on updates.\n\n***\n\n👤 **Organizer:** Mathew\nQuestio
 ns? Post on the event wall or email\n📧 **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotma
 il.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n**Come for the cool
  tunnels.**\n**Stay for the skyline views.**\n**Leave with a BeaverTail in
  hand and the waterfront at sunset.** 🌆🍁🌊
