SUMMARY:🌿🌊 TORONTO ISLANDS SUMMER WALK (9KM) 🌊🌿
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🌿🌊 TORONTO ISLANDS SUMMER 
 WALK (9KM) 🌊🌿\n\n### Island Paths\, Skyline Views & Toronto's Best U
 rban Escape\n\nThere is something magical about the Toronto Islands.\nJust
  minutes from downtown\, the noise of the city disappears and is replaced 
 by tree-lined paths\, open green spaces\, quiet cottages\, and some of the
  best skyline views anywhere in Toronto. It feels like you've escaped the 
 city without ever leaving it.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed summer walk across 
 the Toronto Islands as we explore **Hanlan's Point\, Centre Island\, and W
 ard's Island**\, enjoying beautiful scenery\, fresh air\, and great conver
 sation along the way.\n\nThe Toronto Islands have a fascinating history. O
 riginally connected to the mainland as a long sandbar peninsula\, a powerf
 ul storm in 1858 permanently separated the land from Toronto\, creating th
 e islands we know today.\nOver the years they've been home to amusement pa
 rks\, summer cottages\, and the unique island community that still exists 
 today on Ward's Island.\n\nThis is **not** a formal historical tour.\n\nIt
 's a social walk with beautiful scenery\, fresh air\, and great conversati
 on.\n\n📲 **Don't Forget to join our WhatsApp Group – \\[CLICK HERE\\!
 \\]\\(📲 Join Our WhatsApp Group: Click here to join\\)**\n\n***\n\n## 
 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll take the **11:15 AM Hanlan's Point Fe
 rry** to the islands and begin our walk.\n\nOur route will take us through
 :\n\n🌿 Hanlan's Point\n🌳 Centre Island\n🏡 Ward's Island\n📸 Sev
 eral incredible skyline viewpoints\n🌊 Beautiful waterfront pathways\n\n
 We'll stop throughout the walk to enjoy the scenery for a 30mins break\, t
 ake photos\, and experience one of Toronto's most unique parks.\nFeel free
  to bring a snack or something small to share during one of our breaks.\n\
 n**Please Note:** Although we'll pass several beaches\, we won't be stoppi
 ng at them during this event. We have a route to follow and a ferry to cat
 ch! Instead\, we'll enjoy our break at one of the islands' spectacular sky
 line lookout points\, where you can relax\, have a snack\, and take some a
 mazing photos. If you'd rather spend time at the beach\, you're welcome to
  do so after the walk\, but the group won't be waiting as we continue on o
 ur planned route.\n\nOur return ferry will be the **2:45 PM Ward's Island 
 Ferry** back to downtown Toronto.\n\nExpect approximately **3½ to 4 hours
 ** including the ferry rides and breaks.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Exp
 ectations\n\nThis event happens in typical summer weather.\nThe islands ar
 e often cooler and breezier than downtown Toronto\, so bringing a light sw
 eater is never a bad idea.\nThe only reason we would cancel is because of 
 severe weather or thunderstorms.\n\nThis is a social walk—not a guided h
 istorical tour. I'll share interesting facts along the way\, but the focus
  is enjoying the islands together.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n**
 📍 Meetup Location:**\n**INSIDE the Jack Layton Ferry Terminal after you
 r ticket has been scanned.**\n\nWe are meeting **inside** the paid waiting
  area **beside the washrooms**.\n**Please do NOT wait outside the terminal
 .**\n\nOnce your ferry ticket has been scanned\, walk into the waiting are
 a and you'll find me beside the washrooms wearing my **Moose Hat**.\n\n⏰
  **Meetup Time:** **11:00 AM**\n🚢 **Hanlan's Point Ferry LEAVES AT:** *
 *11:15 AM**\n\nOnce we board the ferry\, it is extremely difficult for lat
 e arrivals to catch up with the group.\n🚢 **Return Ferry:** **2:45 PM f
 rom Ward's Island**\n🎟️ **Ferry Ticket:** *$9.40*\n\nYou must purchas
 e your ferry ticket before signing up.\n[CLICK HERE FOR TICKETS!](https://
 secure.toronto.ca/FerryTicketOnline/tickets2/index.jsp)\n\n***\n\n## 🎟
 ️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **[mathewmacle
 an@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\n\nThis fee helps supp
 ort the group and allows us to continue organizing events like this. Thank
  you for supporting community! 💖\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n
 💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥨 A snack\n🧥 A light swe
 ater\n🕶️ Sunglasses\n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n\n***\n\n## 
 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis group is open to anyone who wants to be soci
 al and make friends—whether single or not.\n\nWe also host:\n🎬 Movies
 \n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture outings\n🍽️ Restaurant gath
 erings\nThere's always something happening.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBER:** You're
  welcome to just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\
 nSometimes plans change and events may need to be cancelled\, so please ke
 ep an eye on updates.\n\n***\n\n👤 **Organizer:** Mathew\nQuestions? Pos
 t on the event wall or email\n📧 **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com]
 (mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**\n\n**Come for the island pa
 ths.**\n**Stay for the skyline.**\n\n**Leave feeling like you spent the da
 y on vacation—without ever leaving Toronto.** 🌿🌊
